    "faq": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "accordion_FVnewG": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does Stride offer the same medical quality as going to a Podiatrist?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes! And in many ways better. Just like in the clinic, you capture a 3D foot scan, record a gait analysis, and answer key questions about your foot health. You can even request a 1:1 consultation with a member of the Stride team. All this in just 5 minutes and a fraction of the cost.</p><p>Your information is then analyzed by our podiatrists who then craft your custom orthotics, designed to alleviate your pain and improve your health.<br/><br/>Don't take our word for it... Stride is <a href=\"/pages/medical-partner\" title=\"Medical Partner\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\"><strong>Prescribed</strong></span></a> by doctors at top podiatry clinics worldwide.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_R94ct4": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Why not use a foam impression box?",
            "answer": "<p><a href=\"/pages/comparison\" title=\"Comparison\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\"><strong>Studies</strong></span></a> show 3D smartphone scans are more accurate & more effective at treating foot pain.</p><p>Plus without back and forth shipping, get your orthotics weeks faster! </p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_6wcntF": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "When/How do I scan my feet & provide the gait video?",
            "answer": "<p>After completing your purchase, we will send you detailed instructions to your email to begin the scan and gait recording process. <br/><br/>The entire process takes around 5 minutes. If you require additional assistance email us at team@stridesoles.com. </p><p>All steps can be completed with an iOS or Android Device. </p><p><a href=\"/pages/how-it-works\" title=\"How it Works\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\"><strong>Learn more</strong></span></a></p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_iTjUYJ": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What if I don't like my Stride Soles?",
            "answer": "<p>If your orthotics aren't right, we'll remake them until they are -- at no extra cost. Still not satisfied? Return them within 180 days for a full refund. </p><p>Less than 1% of customers ever ask for a refund.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_aFH98h": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "I have a diagnosis or orthotics from my Podiatrist. Will you work with me?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes of course! In the open-ended portion of the questionnaire please enter your prescription/information and we will build your orthotics accordingly.<br/><br/>You may also send any documents to team@stridesoles.com with subject \"Podiatrist Review\".</p><p>Finally, if you want an exact replica of your existing orthotics, we have the ability to provide that service for an additional $25 USD. Please write us at team@stridsoles.com for more information.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_ggcL4q": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Does insurance cover Stride?",
            "answer": "<p>We currently accept HSA/FSA cards, as well as doctor notes indicating patient need.<br/><br/>Unfortunately, most insurance companies do not cover custom orthotics, so we do not partner with any.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_dUXgY4": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How long until I feel relief?",
            "answer": "<p>For 80% of patients, relief is immediate as your arches get the needed support.<br/><br/>For others, relief is gradual over two weeks as your body gets used to the support and improved gait mechanics.</p><p>Note: At first, wearing custom orthotics may feel funny or even leave you a bit sore. This is completely normal and evidence that the orthotics are working -- and not just gel cushions from a department store.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_LcEfzh": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How long do Stride last?",
            "answer": "<p>Stride Soles will last 3-5 years, depending on patient weight and usage.</p><p>All custom orthotics come with a 3 year quality guarantee. If the product is damaged within that period, simply reach out to us and we will replace your orthotics, free of charge.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_yzB9VB": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What shoes do Stride fit?",
            "answer": "<p>Stride provides custom orthotics for the following shoe types:</p><ul><li>Dress Shoes</li><li>Sneakers</li><li>Boots</li><li>Running </li><li>Basketball</li><li>Pickleball</li><li>Golf </li><li>Soccer</li></ul>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_9EAfzF": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "When will my Stride Soles arrive?",
            "answer": "<p>Stride Soles custom orthotics will arrive in 10-15 days. This includes production and shipping. </p><p>Need your orthotics sooner? We also offer Express (7-10 days) and Skip the Line (3-5 days) upgrades at checkout.</p>"
          }
        },
        "accordion_nWaKfb": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What conditions do your orthotics help with?",
            "answer": "<p>Custom orthotics are a first line treatment for flat feet, plantar fasciitis, ankle instability, arthritis, pronation, supination, limb-length discrepancy, morton’s neuroma, fractured bones, patellofemoral syndrome, posterior tibialis syndrome, and many other musculoskeletal conditions.</p><p>Strides are more than just a medical treatment. Our insoles are specifically designed to prevent injury by correcting postural issues before injuries occur.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
